         "heading": "Brian Chesky's explanation of changing product management at Airbnb",
         "content": "We don't have any longer the traditional product management function as it existed when you were here. But we didn't get rid of people helping drive the product. What we did is we combined what one might call the inbound product development responsibilities of product manager with the outbound or marketing responsibilities of product marketing.",
         "citation_ids": ["S8"]
      },
      {
         "heading": "Reorganization of product managers at Airbnb",
         "content": "The second thing we did is we off boarded much of the program management functions that product managers may do to actual program managers. ... The last thing we did is we made the group smaller and more senior. So we don't really have a lot of junior product marketers.",
